	(text "Two 8×12 mm ENIG pads on the bottom of the plate; a 2-wire lead from J2 (JST XH) goes\nto J203 on the robot main board (pin 1 = +12 V, pin 2 = GND). The plate is not wired to the\ndock circuit: it is a separate break-away part of the same panel."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 226.06 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2b5155c6-3846-52ed-93d6-1283bf619940")
	)
	(text "NOTES\n• Adapter: 12 V, ≥ 2.5 A, 5.5×2.1 mm barrel, centre positive.\n• The robot reverses onto the dock: the pogo pins press on the\n  contact plate from below (working height 9 mm).\n• Robot side: BQ25798 VAC2 behind a back-to-back FET pair;\n  the charger connects it only once 12 V is valid.\n• Firmware: IINDPM ≤ 2.5 A on VAC2 (two pogo pairs).\n• Finish: ENIG (flat, corrosion-resistant contact pads).\n• Docking alignment: AprilTag on the dock back wall (Pi camera)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 279.4 152.4 0)
		(effects
